course: dictionary
lesson: 2608
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Depression can mean a feeling of illness, a hollow place in the ground, an area of low air pressure in the weather, or a long time with little work and money. «Sadness that lasts many days and takes away the fun of things you loved can be an illness called depression.» The clues are sadness and illness, so here it means an illness of the mind.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «a hollow in the ground» fit «water filled the depression in the field»? Yes, so that meaning works there. Always read the words around the word first.
explain: Depression as an illness is serious, but it is never a child's fault. «Illness is never a child's fault: not a quarrel, not a bad thought, not something you forgot to do caused it.» If sadness lasts for days, tell a parent, teacher or doctor, because it can be helped.
fact: Depression has several meanings, and the context shows which one is meant.
fact: As an illness, depression means feeling very sad, empty, tired or hopeless for a long time, much more than ordinary sadness.
fact: A depression can also be a hollow or low place in a surface, like a dip in the ground where water collects.
fact: In weather, a depression is an area of low air pressure that often brings clouds, wind and rain.
fact: Depression as an illness is not laziness and it is not your fault; doctors and counsellors can help.
exercise: «Depression is an illness, not laziness, and doctors can help.» What is depression in this sentence? | *An illness of the mind that makes a person feel very sad and tired | A long time with no work | A hollow in the ground | An area of low air pressure
exercise: The forecast says «a depression is bringing wind and rain tonight.» What does depression mean here? | A time when many people have no jobs | A feeling of being very sad | A deep hole in a field | *An area of low air pressure that brings clouds, wind and rain
exercise: Pupils are learning about «the Great Depression» in history. What does it mean? | *A long time when many people have no work and little money | A dip in the road | Rainy, windy weather | Sad school days
test: «A parent's drinking, depression or bad mood is never the child's fault.» What does this sentence tell you? | *A child is never to blame for a parent's illness | A child must fix a parent's mood | Depression is a kind of weather | Children can cause a parent's depression
test: If sadness lasts many days and takes away the fun of things you loved, what is the best thing to do? | Blame yourself for being lazy | Keep it secret and wait | Hide from everyone | *Tell a parent, teacher or doctor
exam: Which sentence uses «depression» to mean a hollow place? | *After the rain, water filled a small depression in the field | Depression is an illness that makes you feel empty | A depression is a long time with little money | The Great Depression ended in the 1940s
